1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,898
This is Calzone.

2
00:00:00,898 --> 00:00:02,807
It is part of our HelloVitals app.

3
00:00:02,807 --> 00:00:06,455
Take a picture of your food, and Calzone tells you what is in it.

4
00:00:07,155 --> 00:00:09,469
Keeping track of what you eat is hard.

5
00:00:09,469 --> 00:00:11,174
In space, it is even harder.

6
00:00:11,174 --> 00:00:15,315
NASA found that astronauts on the space station ate too little food.

7
00:00:15,315 --> 00:00:19,516
They also need more vitamin D, because there is no sunlight in space.

8
00:00:19,516 --> 00:00:21,830
And they have to be careful with iron.

9
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:24,715
On the iPhone, open the Calzone tab.

10
00:00:24,715 --> 00:00:29,450
You can use smart glasses, take a photo, or upload a picture you already have.

11
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:33,101
A computer program called an AI looks at the plate.

12
00:00:33,101 --> 00:00:37,209
In about six seconds, it lists each food and guesses how much there is.

13
00:00:37,909 --> 00:00:39,779
But the AI can make mistakes.

14
00:00:39,779 --> 00:00:41,521
Here it said chicken curry.

15
00:00:41,521 --> 00:00:43,391
It was really a cheese curry.

16
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:47,197
So you check each food, and pick the right one from a list.

17
00:00:47,897 --> 00:00:49,123
Now for the numbers.

18
00:00:49,123 --> 00:00:52,741
They come from a big government food list, not from the AI.

19
00:00:52,741 --> 00:00:54,396
Each nutrient has two bars.

20
00:00:54,396 --> 00:00:56,419
One shows what you need on Earth.

21
00:00:56,419 --> 00:00:58,810
The other shows what you need in space.

22
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:00,250
Look at iron.

23
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:04,178
On Earth, this plate gives about a quarter of what you need in a day.

24
00:01:04,178 --> 00:01:06,569
In space, it is already half of the limit.

25
00:01:07,269 --> 00:01:08,858
Add the plate to your day.

26
00:01:08,858 --> 00:01:13,074
Calzone adds up everything you eat, on the phone and on the computer.

27
00:01:13,774 --> 00:01:16,250
Calzone also works on a computer web page.

28
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:20,554
You can upload pictures, and find real science papers about each vitamin.

29
00:01:21,254 --> 00:01:27,071
Everything runs on our own computer, so it works without the internet, just like on a spaceship.

30
00:01:27,071 --> 00:01:29,009
And your pictures are not saved.

31
00:01:29,709 --> 00:01:34,192
We used AI to help build Calzone, and this voice is made by AI too.

32
00:01:34,192 --> 00:01:34,727
Calzone:

33
00:01:34,727 --> 00:01:37,604
look at your plate, and know what is in it.
